==Old English==

===Etymology===
Common Germanic: cognate with Old Saxon [[skakan]], Old Norse [[skaka]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'ʃacan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
'''scacan''' (Class VI strong)

# {{intransitive}} to [[pass]] or [[depart]]
# {{intransitive}} to [[quiver]] or [[vibrate]]
# {{transitive}} to [[flourish]] or [[wave]] (an object)
# {{transitive}} to cause something to [[quiver]], [[flutter]], or [[shake]]

===Descendants===
Modern English [[shake]]

